cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use KOVA3, please cite the resource and state the release version used."
title: "Korean Variant Archive 3 (KOVA3)"
abstract: >-
  KOVA3 is an openly licensed, population-level allele-frequency resource for the
  Korean population, published as an aggregate sites-only layer (allele counts,
  allele numbers, allele frequencies, homozygote counts, call rates, filters, and
  callability) derived from a uniformly joint-genotyped whole-genome callset.
type: dataset
license: CC-BY-4.0
url: "https://github.com/ku-choi-lab/kova3"
# Uncomment once the Registry of Open Data entry is merged and live. Until then
# the URL returns 404 and would render as a dead link on the citation card.
# repository: "https://registry.opendata.aws/kova3/"
# `version` and `date-released` are deliberately absent: they are optional in
# CFF 1.2.0, and a placeholder value would make this file invalid and break the
# "Cite this repository" button. Add both at the first release.
# TODO: add a dataset DOI (for example a Zenodo deposit) at the first release.
authors:
  - name: "Choi Lab, Korea University College of Medicine"
    website: "https://choi.korea.ac.kr/"
contact:
